erstand biodiversity  I geo sites besides us you're working  Amazonia you really wanted father's  getting site based my reversal settings  own i guess my question would be in  order to sort of bulk up my observation  is your validity really understand  what's happening serve it what can we do  better can ray those site networks bring  a comprehensive hold please now the  screen efforts to observe biodiversity  so i suppose we could think of a sort of  a green biodiversity peace corps right  you know part of part of what we just  simply have to deal with is being  content to act on the information we  have because you really are in the end  game in a number of ways and you know  the number of protected areas that will  be created after the next decade or so  will be pretty small which means it's  hugely important for us not only to be  focusing on that but focusing on the  larger landscape and i think we really  need to emphasize the importance of  integrating protected areas into a  larger landscape that has connections in  it so that species can move around you  know like the joshua trees or marching  out of Joshua Tree National Park and  then we have to sort of keep thinking  about it as a series of approximations  on successive refining of what we think  needs to be done to sort of the face of  both the terrestrial part of the planet  but also the marine  well let's thank Tom and the rest of the  speakers for this afternoon session

